OL,3,GNEWSAInside the Met's biggest stolen
OL,4,Agoods crackdown
OL,5,
OL,6,FOne of the largest crackdowns on the
OL,7,Fresale of stolen goods has been carried
OL,8,Fout by the Metropolitan Police.
OL,10,FOfficers visited about 400 shops,
OL,11,Fmarket stalls and car boot sales,
OL,12,Fleading to 42 arrests and 11 closure
OL,13,Forders for shops.
OL,15,FDeputy Commissioner Matt Jukes said
OL,16,Fabout 100 prolific shoplifters were
OL,17,Fresponsible for 4,000 offences across
OL,18,FLondon and the force was "going up the
OL,19,Ffood chain" to target the businesses
OL,20,Fand criminals profiting from theft.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,324,320,200,140,0,100
